cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this measurement or its figures, please cite it as below."
title: "psrtype-samfyring — ENTSO-E's schema permits multiple production types per generation unit; in four zones with documented co-firing, none is reported"
abstract: >-
  ENTSO-E's GL_MarketDocument schema places TimeSeries at 1..unbounded per
  document, each carrying exactly one psrType, with no uniqueness constraint on
  the generating unit mRID. Two TimeSeries for the same unit with different
  production types are therefore schema-valid. Across 1 497 documents covering
  238 generation units in four bidding zones where biomass co-firing is
  documented in a dated primary source for 2021-2024 -- Finland, Poland, the
  Netherlands and Czechia -- no unit carries two production types in the same
  document. Neither ENTSO-E's Manual of Procedures nor its schema document
  contains any of twelve multi-fuel terms. Criteria were preregistered and
  checksummed before the finding was frozen.
authors:
  - family-names: "Botten Nicolaysen"
    given-names: "Eirik"
